2026-06-12T09:29Z HDMX-coding-agent created

--- body ---
## Context

Adherence tests that pin *positive* prose literals ("abstract must contain
'point toward a working hypothesis'") break on every legitimate authorial
rewrite and force test-chasing edits (bit on PR #1014, the 2026-06-12
abstract rewrite: two tests pinned sentences of the superseded draft).
The asymmetry: pinning what must be said requires NLP; forbidding what
must NOT be said works with literals, because defects (overclaim
signature phrases, hand-typed numbers, hardcoded refs) are lexically
stable while prose is not.

Policy decided with the author (2026-06-12 session):
1. CI keeps only mechanical guards + *negative* guards (forbidden-phrasing
   ratchets for claims reviews ruled overclaimed).
2. Positive semantic intent moves to review-time: an editorial-brief file
   listing standing editorial decisions (claim X stays hedged, abstract
   leads with the difficulty result, ...) that the /review-pr-prose panel
   checks each manuscript diff against.

## Relevant files

- `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` — mixed: hedging guards on
  conclusion/body still pin positive literals ("suggests the binding
  constraint lies", "appears to shift from model capability", "the
  evidence points toward a conjecture about why", ...)
- `tests/test_manuscript_structure.py` — structure (keep) + frontier
  framing (already loosened on PR #1014; demote further or keep as-is)
- `tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py`, `tests/test_manuscript_macros.py`,
  `tests/test_abstract_numbers*.py`, `tests/test_no_inline_plots.py` —
  mechanical, KEEP unchanged
- `.claude/skills/review-pr-prose/` (user-level IDH skill: check
  `~/.claude/skills/review-pr-prose/SKILL.md`) — add brief-check step
- New: `docs/editorial-brief.md` — the standing-decisions list

## Actions

1. Inventory every assertion in the manuscript prose test files; classify
   mechanical / negative / positive-literal.
2. For each positive literal: rewrite as a negative guard where the
   underlying decision was "never state X flatly"; otherwise move the
   decision into `docs/editorial-brief.md` (cite the originating ticket:
   0532, 0541, author briefs) and delete the assertion.
3. Create `docs/editorial-brief.md`; each entry = decision + rationale +
   originating ticket.
4. Wire the brief into the prose review path so manuscript PRs are checked
   against it (skill edit may need an IDH-side PR; if so, file a companion
   ticket there and reference it here).

## Test

- Adherence meta-test: grep the prose test files for `in abstract`/`in
  conclusion`-style *positive* literal assertions and fail if any remain
  outside an allowlist (the red step: write it first, watch it list the
  current offenders).

## Verification

- [ ] `make check` green
- [ ] A trial rewording of a hedged sentence (same meaning, different
  words) no longer fails CI
- [ ] Reintroducing "the binding constraint is the documents" flatly in
  the abstract DOES fail CI

## Invariants

- Mechanical guards (crossref, macros, numbers-from-artifacts, inline
  plots, JSON EOF) unchanged.
- Negative guards never weakened — each existing overclaim ratchet maps to
  a negative guard or a brief entry, none silently dropped.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No positive prose-literal assertion remains in CI
- [ ] `docs/editorial-brief.md` exists and carries every demoted decision
- [ ] Prose review path references the brief
